-**RF-1 — `audit_logs` already exists in a different shape (AC-102, AC-104, AC-105).** `0015_audit_logs.sql:10-33` created it: uuid PK, `username NOT NULL`, `record_id varchar(128)`, `field_name`, `old_value/new_value text`, free-text `action`, `ip_address`, `user_agent`, `created_at/updated_at`, three different indexes, a `set_updated_at` trigger. The pack writes as if the table is new. `0015` is read-only, so the only literal path to AC-102's eleven columns is **drop + recreate in `0028`** (assert empty first). No data exists anywhere: dev backend is at the 2-table baseline (VG-8); throwaways are wiped from scratch. `RLS_TEMPLATES.md:179` already assigns this table to BIM-003. **Ask:** ratify drop + recreate (recommended). ALTER-in-place cannot produce AC-102's column order or PK type without dropping every column anyway.
