-**RF-4 — AC-303 / AC-304 literal golden.** Every run regenerates uuids (`gen_random_uuid()`, `auth.admin.createUser`) and `old_data/new_data` carry `created_at/updated_at`. A committed file with literal uuids can never match. **Proposal:** golden carries **symbolic** tokens (`"business_id": "A1"`, `"actor_user_id": "admin-A"`, `"row_id": "<uuid>"`); the runner maps real ids → symbols via the seed map before diffing; `old_data/new_data` compared as null/non-null plus a whitelisted stable key set; comparison scoped to rows with `id >` a watermark taken **before** the scripted session (seed writes ~600 rows of `postgres`-actor noise). AC-304 "uuid or null" → erratum wording "symbol or null".
